Elwand RT2800 USB helper
========================

This directory contains the runtime helper `rt2800d`, its firmware and the
corresponding source code.

Source code
-----------
The complete source for `rt2800d` ships with Elwand in:

    src/data/rt2800/source/

It is also part of the source distribution (`sdist`) and the installed package
(`site-packages/src/data/rt2800/source/`). If a redistribution omits it, the
corresponding source can be obtained from the Elwand repository or from the
maintainer on request.

License
-------
`rt2800d` is a separate executable derived from the Linux `rt2x00` /
`rt2800usb` driver (GPL-2.0) and a macOS userspace port. The full license text
is in `COPYING` (GPL-2.0) and in `source/COPYING`. Some host files carry an
SPDX dual license (GPL-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause) as stated in their file headers.

The Elwand Python application invokes `rt2800d` as a separate process; it is
not linked into the Python interpreter.

Firmware
--------
`rt2870.bin` is Ralink/MediaTek firmware redistributed under the terms in
`ralink-firmware.txt` and `source/LICENSES/ralink-firmware.txt`.

Build
-----
    make -C src/data/rt2800/source/port install

This requires macOS, Xcode Command Line Tools (clang) and the IOKit /
CoreFoundation frameworks. The shipped binary is built for Apple Silicon
(arm64); the source is provided so other architectures can rebuild it.

Build provenance
----------------
See `BUILD_INFO` for the source location, binary SHA-256, build command and
architecture of the shipped helper.

